Three options fit a route this small:

| Option | Size | Types | Errors |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Hand-written | None | Manual | Our own list |
| Zod | Larger | Inferred | Path and message |
| Valibot | Small | Inferred | Path and message |

For three fields the hand-written check is enough, and it keeps the project free of dependencies:

```ts
export function validate(body: SignUp): Problem[] {
  const problems: Problem[] = [];
  if (!body.name?.trim()) problems.push({ field: "name", code: "required" });
  if (!/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/.test(body.email ?? "")) problems.push({ field: "email", code: "invalid" });
  if (!config.trails.includes(body.trail)) problems.push({ field: "trail", code: "unknown" });
  return problems;
}
```

If the request grows past a handful of fields, Valibot gives the same kind of errors in a smaller bundle.

